================================================================================
2. Dataset — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
================================================================================

Applies to: terceira_caves.csv, cavedata.js, cave_entrances.json,
terceira_caves.gpx, photos.js (the caption and attribution records, not the
image files), sigcava_terceira_merged.geojson and RESEARCH.md.

Compilation © 2026 Xavier Francisco, licensed under CC BY 4.0
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>.

Suggested attribution: "Terceira Caves dataset, Xavier Francisco,
https://github.com/Qu4tro/terceira-caves, CC BY 4.0".

The compilation is derived from official and published sources that carry
their own attribution requirements — see "Data sources" in README.md. In
particular, coordinates, classes and scores originate from SIGCAVA (Governo
dos Açores — Secretaria Regional do Ambiente e Ação Climática, Direção
Regional do Ambiente e Ação Climática) and from Resolução do Conselho do
Governo n.º 163/2024; fauna records derive from Borges et al. (2019),
Biodiversity Data Journal 7: e32530 (CC BY 4.0) and the GBIF dataset "Azorean
Cave Arthropods".

================================================================================
3. Photographs — individually licensed third-party works
================================================================================

Applies to: everything under photos/.

Each image is a third-party work from Wikimedia Commons, used under its own
licence (public domain, CC0, CC BY, or CC BY-SA). The photographer credit,
licence and source page for every file are recorded in photos.js and rendered
alongside the image in the application. Images under CC BY-SA remain under
CC BY-SA; nothing in this file relicenses them.

================================================================================
4. Primary documents — third-party material, rights reserved by their owners
================================================================================

Applies to: everything under sources/ and the remaining raw files under
sigcava_raw/.

These are archival copies of the primary documents and raw data extracts
behind the dataset, kept for verifiability. Rights remain with their
respective publishers and authors:

- resolucao_163_2024.pdf and dlr_10_2019A.pdf are official legal texts of the
  Regional Government of the Azores (Jornal Oficial), which are not subject to
  copyright protection as official texts.
- sources/bdj2019/ derives from Borges et al. (2019), Biodiversity Data
  Journal 7: e32530, CC BY 4.0.
- sources/borges1994/ reproduces Borges, Pereira & Silva (1994), "Grutas e
  Algares dos Açores. I", Actas do 3.º Congresso Nacional de Espeleologia, for
  scholarly documentation. All rights remain with the authors.
- sigcava_raw/ contains extracts of SIGCAVA GIS data, © Governo dos Açores.
